interpreters/rust/target/

# N Lang Snapp intermediate build output — regenerate with `nlang export`.
# The compiler writes to build/ despite the config naming .n/build, so both
# are listed. The exported bundle under snapp/ IS tracked: it is the
# artifact other Snapps consume.
#
# These patterns are GENERIC, not per-Snapp, and that is the point. They were
# `APH Spec/0.1.0/build/` until a second Snapp was added and its build cache
# was not covered — roughly five hundred lines of absolute developer paths and
# sibling-project names, staged for a public repository, caught one command
# before the commit. A path-specific ignore silently stops protecting the
# moment someone adds a sibling, and nothing announces the gap: the sanitize
# job scans TRACKED files, so the leak only becomes visible after it is
# already committed. Keep these generic. Adding a Snapp must not require
# remembering to add a line here.
**/build/
**/.n/build/
**/.n/wal/
